{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `#lang conscript` base includes html.rkt which has `@form` and `@button`. There's also `conscript/form0` with widgets like `@input-text[#:name]` and `@~error[#:name]`, used via `require conscript/form0`.\n\nNow, the `defstep` body — steps run, and within a step you can have form actions that call `set!` on defvar variables, or use `#:action on-submit` callbacks. Let me look at how the example does validation of non-empty input.\n\nThe example in `/reference/conscript/examples/form.rkt` uses:\n\n```racket\n(defstep (the-form)\n  (define (on-submit #:name n #:text t)\n    ...)\n\n  @html{@h1{The Form}\n        @form[#:action on-submit]{\n          @label{Name: @input-text[#:name] @~error[#:name]}\n          @textarea[#:text]{Content:}\n          @submit-button}})\n```\n\nHmm, wait — this uses `html`? Actually in conscript examples, they may use haml from koyo. Let me check the html.rkt to see what @html, @form, @button are. Also check `input-text` required? behavior for non-empty: In the congame reference for `input-text`, `#:required? req` default #t means field must contain data before submission. But is whitespace-only considered empty? \"non-empty display name\" — I should trim and validate manually too.\n\nLet me look at the conscript reference docs for `form` and inputs within `#lang conscript` proper (conscript-reference.scrbl). Also check `html.rkt`.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"So\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" `\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"#\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"lang\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" cons\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"cript\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\