{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":269,"output":1132,"cacheRead":56192,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1106,"totalTokens":57593,"cost":{"input":0.000020175,"output":0.000283,"cacheRead":0.00084288,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.001146055}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Good\n\n\n:\n\n missing\n\n \n\n `\n\n_\n\n_\n\ntt\n\n\n`\n/\n`\n\n_\n\n_\n\nft\n\n\n`\n\n defaults\n\n\n to\n\n \n\n `\n\n\n#f\n`\n\n —\n\n\n no\n\n \n\n error\n.\n\n\n I\n\n\n can\n\n\n still\n\n\n send\n\n\n them\n\n\n (\n0\n)\n to\n\n \n\n be\n\n \n\n realistic\n.\n\n\n\nNow\n\n\n\n \n\n\nlet\n\n\n me\n\n\n write\n\n\n the\n\n\n study\n.\n\n\n Final\n\n\n design\n:\n\n\n\n```\nr\n\n\nacket\n\n\n#\nlang\n\n\n cons\n\n\ncript\n\n\n\n(\nrequire\n\n\n cons\n\n\ncript\n/form0\n\n\n         racket\n/string\n)\n\n\n(pro\nvide\n\n\n benchmark\n-st\nudy\n)\n\n\n(defvar\n display\n-name\n)\n\n\n(def\nstep\n (\nint\nroduction\n)\n\n \n @\nmd\n*\n{\n\n\n   #\n Benchmark\n Study\n\n\n\n   Welcome!\n This\n study\n asks\n you\n a\n few\n simple\n questions\n.\n\n\n   @\nbutton\n{\nContinue\n}})\n)\n\n\n;\n Rejects\n names\n that\n are\n empty\n (or\n whitespace-only).\n\n\n(define\n ((non-empty-string-v #:message [msg \"Please enter your name.\"]) v)\n\n \n (cond\n\n   \n [(and (string? v) (non-empty? (string-trim v)))\n    (cons 'ok (string-trim v))]\n\n   \n [else (cons 'err msg)]))\n\n\n(defstep (display-name-step)\n\n \n (define-values (the-form on-submit)\n   (form+submit\n    [display-name\n     (ensure binding/text\n             (required)\n             (non-empty-string-v))]))\n\n\n \n (define (render rw)\n\n   \n @md*{\n\n     # What is your name?\n\n\n     Please type your name below.  You can't continue with an empty name.\n\n\n     @rw[\"display-name\" (input-text)]\n\n     @|submit-button|})\n\n\n \n @md*{\n\n   # Your Name\n\n   @form[the-form on-submit render]})\n\n\n(defstep (finished)\n\n \n @md*{\n\n   # All done!\n\n   Thank you, **@|display-name|**! Your responses have been recorded.\n\n\n   @button{Finish}})\n\n\nHmm wait - \"final page includes the submitted name\". A button on final page would loop or move on... Since it's terminal, adding @button{Finish} makes clicking re-render same page. That's typical (kitchen-sink's done has no button; form.rkt's done none either). But TASK says intro must have Continue button; final just needs to include name. No button needed. But then how does congame mark completion... Let me keep it simple without a button on final step, matching curated examples' done steps.\n\n\nActually, wait: display via @|display-name| inside md. Need escaping of user content? Markdown rendering inserts raw string. Fine for exercise; but XSS-wise congame likely escapes? Not our concern here.\n\n\nAlso note: (defvar display-name) then form+submit binder syntax: [display-name (ensure ...)] sets that var directly. Then in finished step, @|display-name| refers to var value.\n\n\nEdge: what does form+submit do on validation error - re-renders form with errors visible. rw rendering shows widget errors near field automatically? The widgets receive errors as third arg and render ul.errors next to input? Actually widget-text renders only input; error display requires explicit @~error[...] style markers? In cookbook render they didn't add error placeholders, but forms-lib widget-input ignores _errors... Hmm widget-input takes name binding _errors and doesn't render them. So how do errors show? In form.rkt example they used @~error[#:name] markers. ~error comes from congame components formular (prefix). Hmm, actually in conscript/form0 provide list: ~error not listed! form0 provides from congame formular: ~error? Looking at form0 provide: (rename-out [form+combine form] [congame:formular-autofill bot:autofill] [congame:submit-button submit-button]) form+submit dyn:form make-autofill errors checkbox input-date... required-unless at-least number-in-range list-longer-than make-autofill-meta. No ~error export. The html-element define-elements in html-element.rkt defines custom elements like @~error? form.rkt example uses @~error[#:name] with @form[#:action on-submit]{...} which resembles koyo/haml-based new element system in base's html.rkt? html-elements defined list didn't include ~error though. That example may target a newer version than installed here? Careful.\n\n\nTo be safe: use cookbook recipe exactly (it's from current docs): form+submit + ensure + render via @md*/@rw + submit-button. Validation errors: forms-lib's form-run collects errors; where displayed? Possibly nowhere unless using widget-errors explicitly. We can include (errors \"name\" value errlist)? form0 exports `errors` procedure: (define (errors name value errors) ...) line 106. It returns xexpr with error messages. Signature from forms private widget: widget-errors: (-> name value errors xexpr?) when curried: ((errors name) value errs)? Hmm let me check form0/errors definition lines 106-108: (define (errors name value errors) ...) — need to view.\n\n\nLet me read form0 lines around 78-115."}}
