{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":2,"delta":"{\"path\":\"/workspace/exercise.rkt\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env racket\\n;; Exercises the benchmark-study against a running Congame server by walking\\n;; the participant flow over HTTP:\\n;;\\n;;   1. Anon login for the instance (intro page with Continue).\\n;;   2. Continue -> name-entry page.\\n;;   3. Submitting an empty name must be rejected (still on the form).\\n;;   4. Submitting a real name lands on the final page echoing the name.\\n;;\\n;; Usage: racket exercise.rkt\\n\\n(module+ main\\n  (require racket/list\\n           racket/port\\n           racket/string)\\n\\n  (define base (or (getenv \\\"CONGAME_URL\\\") \\\"http://host.docker.internal:45471\\\"))\\n  (define slug (or (getenv \\\"CONGAME_INSTANCE\\\")\\n                   \\\"bench-20260827t083933z-smoke--fdb568e7\\\"))\\n\\n  ;; ------------------------------------------------------------------ utils\\n\\n  (define failures 0)\\n\\n  (define (check! ok? label)\\n    (printf \\\"~a ~a~n\\\" (if ok? \\\"PASS\\\" \\\"FAIL\\\") label)\\n    (unless ok?\\n      (set! failures (add1 failures))))\\n\\n  ;; Run a program capturing its stdout as a string.\\n  (define (run prog . args)\\n    (define-values (proc stdout stdin stderr ctl)\\n      (apply subprocess #f #f 'stdout prog args))\\n    (close-input-port stdin)\\n    (define out (port->bytes stdout))\\n    (close-input-port stdout)\\n    (subprocess-wait proc)\\n    (values (zero? (subprocess-status proc)) (bytes->string/utf-8 out)))\\n\\n  ;; HTTP requests via curl (handles cookies, follows redirects).\\n  (define jar (make-temporary-file \\\"congame-bench-cookies~a\\\"))\\n  (file-permissions jar #o600)\\n\\n  (define (http req-type url [body-or-false #f])\\n    (define fallback (if (equal? req-type \\\"-F\\\") \\\"--form-string\\\" \\\"--data-urlencode\\\"))\\n    (define success? #f)\\n    (define out\\n      (cond\\n        [body-or-false\\n         (run-values/yield\\n          \\\"/usr/bin/curl\\\"\\n          \\\"-sS\\\" \\\"-i\\\" \\\"-X\\\" req-type fallback body-or-false\\n          \\\"-b\\\" (path->string jar) \\\"-c\\\" (path->string jar)\\n          url)]\\n        [else\\n         (run-values/yield\\n          \\\"/usr/bin/curl\\\"\\n          \\\"-sS\\\" \\\"-i\\\"\\n          \\\"-b\\\" (path->string jar) \\\"-c\\\" (path->string jar)\\n          url)])))\\n\\n  (define (run-values/yield . args)\\n    (let-values (((ok body) (apply run args)))\\n      (set! success? ok)\\n      body))\\n\\n  (define (resolve url)\\n    (if (string-prefix? url \\\"http\\\")\\n        url\\n        (string-append base url)))\\n\\n  ;; Fetch a page, following redirects/refreshes transparently.\\n  (define (fetch-page url)\\n    (define raw (second (http \\\"\\\" (resolve url))))\\n    (raw-body raw))\\n\\n  (define (raw-body res)\\n    (or (for/first ([chunk (in-list (string-split res \\\"\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\"))]\\n                    #:when (string-starts? (car (string-split chunk \\\"\\\\n\\\")) \\\"\\\")\\n                    ; body after blank line\\n                    #f)\\n          chunk)\\n        (last-or-null\\n         (regexp-split #rx\\\"\\\\r?\\\\n\\\\r?\\\\n\\\" res))))\\n\\n  (define (string-starts? s _prefix) #f) ; placeholder, unused\\n\\n  (define (last-or-null l)\\n    (if (null? l) \\\"\\\" (last l)))\\n\\n  ...\\n  )\\n\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":85,"output":3546,"cacheRead":64256,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2699,"totalTokens":67887,"cost":{"input":0.000006375,"output":0.0008864999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0009638399999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0018567149999999997}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The upload succeeded — it printed the study admin URL. (It shows `127.0.0.1:45471` since the configured server base resolved locally; the task said the server is `http://host.docker.internal:45471`, same port.)\n\nNow write `exercise.rkt` to walk through the participant flow over HTTP:\n\n1. GET `http://host.docker.internal:45471/_anon-login/bench-20260827t083933z-smoke--fdb568e7` with a cookie jar.\n2. Follow redirects to the study page; assert intro content (\"Benchmark Study\") and a Continue link (`a.button.next-button`).\n3. GET the continue href → should land on name form; parse `<form action=\"...\">` and input names.\n4. POST empty field (multipart or urlencoded) → expect error message visible, still on form.\n5. POST valid name \"Bench Tester\" → expect redirect then final page containing the name.\n6. Assert final page includes name.\n\nImplementation: use Racket's net/url with cookies? No built-in cookie jar. Options:\n- Use curl via subprocess — much simpler and robust. The task says exercise.rkt is optional but useful. I can implement it in Racket calling curl, or pure Racket HTTP with manual cookie handling.\n\nPure-Racket approach: web-server/http gives parsing; sending requires http-client library... plain `net/url` can send POST and handle headers including Set-Cookie manually. Sessions: auth-manager presumably sets a session cookie (koyo auth middleware). I'll capture all `Set-Cookie` headers and replay them.\n\nLet me write it in pure Racket with net/url:\n\n- GET url → response struct via `(call/input-url ...)`? Need port + headers. Simpler: use `net/url`'s `http-sendrecv/url` which returns input port plus we need headers — `(http-sendrecv/url u ...)` returns (values status headers port)? Actually it returns an input port; there's `net/head`. Use `proxy-ify`? Hmm.\n\nSimplest robust path: shell out to curl from racket with `-c jar -b jar -sS -L --post302`, parse output. But mixing Racket+curl is fine for an exercise harness. However, nicer: do everything in curl within a bash script? The task suggests `racket exercise.rkt` as the command. I'll write exercise.rkt that invokes curl via subprocess for each step. Actually even simpler and fully deterministic: write exercise.rkt in pure Racket using `curl`? Let me think about what's most reliable:\n\nMultipart encoding by hand is annoying; urlencoded forms might not be accepted because form default enctype is multipart/form-data — koyo's continuation handler parses request bindings from any body type? web-server's request-bindings/raw handles both urlencoded and multipart when dispatched... For continuations, koyo uses servlet dispatch on URL; `request-bindings/raw` extracts query + body bindings regardless of content type as long as declared properly? The web server parses both application/x-www-form-urlencoded and multipart/form-data bodies into request-bindings. So posting urlencoded should work fine even though enctype says multipart.\n\nPlan (pure Racket):\n- require net/url, web-server/http (for header parsing?), racket/port, racket/string.\n- Implement get/post functions returning (values status-code headers-string body).\n- Maintain cookie list; append Cookie header on every request; extract set-cookie values from response headers.\n- Step logic:\n  1. GET anon-login URL; it 302s to /study/<slug>. Don't auto-follow; read Location.\n  2. GET location → body intro page. Check contains \"Benchmark Study\" and href with class next-button (parse `href=\"...\"` of the `<a ... up-follow ...>`), follow GET.\n  3. Now at name form: find first `action=\"...\"` inside form tag. Check contains `<form`.\n  4. POST to action with urlencoded body `display-name=` plus maybe __tt/__ft=0 → expect either re-rendered form containing error text (\"Please enter your name.\") — confirm step did NOT advance (page still has `<input`). Note: on failure, response may be 200 with form again.\n     Careful: post-field name: widget key passed was \"display-name\". Good.\n  5. POST again with display-name=Bench Tester (url-encoded) → expect 303/302 redirect (redirect/get/forget/protect returns redirect). GET Location.\n  6. Final page: must contain \"All done!\" and \"Thank you, Bench Tester\" (entity-decoded?). HTML escaping: name has space; xexpr rendering keeps spaces. Check substring \"Bench Tester\".\n  7. Print PASS/FAIL summary; exit code accordingly.\n\nRedirects: use raw handling with manual Location following (max 5).\n\nkoyo auth session: check what cookie name/behavior — login! sets session cookie typically `sid` or similar via set-cookie with HttpOnly etc. Our generic capture handles it.\n\nCSRF: koyo middleware? grep showed no xsrf hits in congame-web root *.rkt only compiled dir search failed earlier (I greped /opt/congame/congame-web/*.rkt top-level, and got nothing). Auth pages didn't reference csrf. Likely no CSRF token needed. Also continuation URLs include integrity hashes rather than tokens. \n\nLet me also double-check how run-study handles GET without button params vs POST to embed/url. The form action embed covers both render & submit: posting runs `(lambda (_req) (response/render this-step))`; form-run sees bindings present & validates... wait: form-run runs against this-request every time, but the 'passed branch only happens after processing POST bindings. On our empty-submit POST, form-run returns ('failed/errors?) branch → renders rw with errors (200 OK, no redirect). Then correct input posts → passes → action sets vars → continue → advance. That matches plan.\n\nOne more concern: timers (__tt/__ft) missing → call-with-timings parameterizes cons(#f,#f); widgets that record timings