{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I\n started\n writing\n that\n and\n it\n got\n messy\n —\n I\n was\n mixing\n approaches\n mid\n-file\n (\nthe\n http\n/\nrun\n-values\n/yield\n split\n is\n broken\n,\n raw\n-body\n regex\n garbage\n).\n Let\n me\n rewrite\n exercise\n.r\nkt\n cleanly\n from\n scratch\n with\n a\n simple\n design\n:\n\n-\n One\n function\n `\nhttp\n-request\n`\n using\n curl\n \n-i\n to\n capture\n full\n response\n (headers+body),\n then\n manually\n follow\n \n30x\n redirect\ns\n up\n to\n N\n hops\n by\n parsing\n `Location\n:`\n headers\n.\n\n-\n Cookie\n jar\n handled\n by\n curl\n (`\n-b\n/`\n-c\n).\n\n-\n Keep\n a\n helper\n to\n grab\n the\n final\n body\n after\n following\n redirects.\n\n\nStructure:\n\n\n```\nracket\n\n\n#lang\n racket\n/base\n\n\n(require\n racket/port\n\n\n        \n racket\n/string\n\n        \n racket\n/file\n\n        \n racket/list)\n\n\n;;\n ---\n config\n\n\n\n(define\n base\n ...)\n\n\n(define\n slug\n ...)\n\n\n;;\n run\n external\n command\n ->\n (values\n ok?\n stdout\n-string\n)\n\n\n;;\n simplest\n correct\n subprocess\n capture\n\n\n(\ndefine\n (\nrun\n prog\n .\n args\n)\n\n \n (\ndefine\n out\n-o\n (\nmake\n-pipe\n))\n\n\n \n ...\n \n\n)`\n\n\nEven\n simpler\n &  bulletproof\n:\n use\n `\nwith\n-output\n-to\n-by\ntes\n`\n wrapping\n `\nsystem\n*`\n with\n arg\n vector\n —\n no\n shell\n quoting\n issues\n,'\nstdout\n captured\n:\n\n``\n`\n\n(require\n racket/system\n)\n\n...\n (\nwith\n-output\n-to\n-by\ntes\n.\n #t\n (λ () (system\n* \"/usr/bin/curl\" \"-sS\" \"-i\" url))\n)\n\n```\n\n`\n\nsystem\n*\n with\n `#t` as last arg waits and returns status.\n `with-output-to-bytes` captures stdout.\n stderr passthrough visible for debug. That's clean.\n\n\nSo:\n\n\n```\nr\nacket\n\n\n#lang\n racket/base\n\n\n(require\n racket/system\n\n\n         \n racket/port\n\n\n         \n racket/string\n\n\n         \n racket/list)\n\n\n(define\n (curl\n . args)\n\n \n (with\n-output-to-bytes\n \n #t\n\n   \n (lambda ()\n (apply system\n* \"/usr/bin/curl\" \"-sS\" \"-i\"\n args))))\n\n\n;; follow redirects manually; returns\n final (headers\n-string body)\n pair-ish\n\n\n(define\n (get-page url)\n\n \n (let\n loop ([n 5] [u url])\n\n   \n (define\n res (curl \"-b\" jar \"-c\" jar u))\n\n   \n (cond [(and (> n 0) (redirect? res)) (loop (- n 1) (location-of res))]\n\n         [else res])))\n```\n\n\nRedirect detection:\n header block before first blank line;\n search\n case-insensitive \"location:\".\n Parse via string-split lines.\n\n\nPOST: `-X POST --data-urlencode display-name=<value>` plus optional `--data-urlencode __tt=0 --data-urlencode __ft=0`. Using -X POST with --data-urlencode alone implies POST anyway.\n\n\nExtract helpers:\n\n- first match regexp on body: `(regexp-match #px\"<a [^>]*href=\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"\" ...)` restricted to next-button anchors. Button attr order: class then href? Let me recall from define/widget button haml:\n\n```\n(:a ([:class (...)] [:up-follow ...] [:up-transition ...] [:data-widget-id ...] [:href embed]))\n```\n\nHTML output order: attributes likely emitted in given order: class=\"button next-button\", up-follow=\".step\", up-transition=\"none\", data-widget-id=(nothing when not bot), href=\"/...\".\n\nRegex: `#px\"a class=\\\"[^\\\"]*next-button[^\\\"]*\\\"[^>]*href=\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"\"` should work if no other attrs between class and href... there are up-follow/up-transition between but [^>]* covers them.\n\n\nForm action extraction: `#px\"<form[^>]*action=\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"\"`.\n\n\nCheck form input name exists: contains `\"display-name\"` substring.\n\n\nAlso possible intro page markup: title text via md; assert substring \"Benchmark Study\" and \"Continue\".\n\n\nName with space in POST value: --data-urlencode handles encoding.\n\n\nEntity decoding: server may escape \"Bench Tester\" → stays same (no special chars). Fine.\n\n\nOne more nuance: after empty POST fails, the re-rendered page includes error message \"Please enter your name.\" — from widget-errors rendering via `(errors name value errors)` inside field-group... wait, I used bare `@rw[\"display-name\" (input-text)]` without label — input-text = make-input-widget which wraps `.field-group` + label + widget + widget-errors. So errors render automatically. Good: assert substring \"Please enter your name.\"\n\n\nEmpty-value semantics: posting `--data-urlencode display-name=` gives binding \"\" (present). binding/text produces \"\"; required passes (\"\", truthy); my validator errs. So error shown — good test of non-empty validation (distinct from missing-field required path).\n\n\nAlso second POST success flow: after action, congame does redirect/get/forget/protect → 303 or 302 with Location; then GET continues → renders finished. My get-page follows Location once more automatically.\n\n\nWhat about Set-Cookie needing re-save across manual loops: each invocation uses both -b and -c so cookies persist through loop.\n\n\nPotential wrinkle: anon-login GET sets session cookie and 302s to /study/<slug>; initial landing GET returns intro HTML with status 200.\n\n\nEdge: continuation URLs contain query params including \"?...\" already; fine.\n\n\nTimeout: add `--max-time 20`.\n\n\nNow rewrite file completely.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"I\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"\\n\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" started\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"\\n\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" writing\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"\\n\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" that\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"\\n\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\