{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":1,"delta":"{\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env racket\\n#lang racket/base\\n\\n;; Exercises benchmark-study against the Congame server over HTTP.\\n;;\\n;; Flow checked:\\n;;   1. Anon login for the active instance -> introduction page w/ Continue.\\n;;   2. Continue -> name entry form.\\n;;   3. Empty name submission is rejected (validation error, stays on form).\\n;;   4. A real submission advances to a final page echoing the submitted name.\\n;;\\n;; Usage: racket exercise.rkt   (exits nonzero on any failure)\\n\\n(module+ main\\n  (require racket/system\\n           racket/list\\n           racket/file\\n           racket/string)\\n\\n  ;; --------------------------------------------------------------- config\\n\\n  (define base (or (getenv \\\"CONGAME_URL\\\")\\n                   \\\"http://host.docker.internal:45471\\\"))\\n  (define slug (or (getenv \\\"CONGAME_INSTANCE\\\")\\n                   \\\"bench-20260827t083933z-smoke--fdb568e7\\\"))\\n\\n  ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- utils\\n\\n  (define failures 0)\\n\\n  (define (check! ok? label)\\n    (printf \\\"~a ~a~n\\\" (if ok? \\\"PASS\\\" \\\"FAIL\\\") label)\\n    (unless ok?\\n      (set! failures (add1 failures))))\\n\\n  ;; Full curl call (response incl. headers due to -i).\\n  (define (curl . args)\\n    (with-output-to-bytes\\n      (lambda ()\\n        (apply system* \\\"/usr/bin/curl\\\" \\\"-sS\\\" \\\"--max-time\\\" \\\"30\\\" args))))\\n\\n  (define jar (make-temporary-file \\\"congame-bench-cookies~a\\\"))\\n  (file-permissions jar #o600)\\n\\n  ;; Split raw response into headers/body.\\n  (define (split-headers-body raw)\\n    (define pos\\n      (match (regexp-match-positions #rx\\\"\\\\r?\\\\n\\\\r?\\\\n\\\" raw)\\n        [(cons start end) end]\\n        [#f (string-length raw)]))\\n    (values (substring raw 0 pos)\\n            (substring raw pos)))\\n\\n  (define (redirect-location raw)\\n    (define-values (headers _body) (split-headers-body raw))\\n    (for/first ([line (in-list (string-split headers \\\"\\\\r\\\\n\\\"))]\\n                #:when (string-prefix? (string-foldcase line) \\\"location:\\\")\\n                #:do [(define target (string-trim (substring line 9)))]\\n                #:when (non-empty-string? target))\\n      (if (string-prefix? target \\\"http\\\")\\n          target\\n          (string-append base target))))\\n\\n  (define (status-code raw)\\n    (define-values (headers _) (split-headers-body raw))\\n    (match (string-trim headers)\\n      [(pregexp \\\"^HTTP[^ ]* ([0-9]+)\\\") (string->number (list-ref '(0 1) 0))]\\n      [_ 0]))\\n\\n  ;; One request with cookies; manually follows up to 6 redirects.\\n  (define (request! method url data-field)\\n    (let loop ([hop 0] [u url])\\n      (define raw\\n        (bytes->string/utf-8\\n         (cond\\n           [data-field\\n            (curl \\\"-X\\\" method \\\"--data-urlencode\\\" data-field\\n                  \\\"-b\\\" (path->string jar) \\\"-c\\\" (path->string jar)\\n                  u)]\\n           [else\\n            (curl \\\"-X\\\" method\\n                  \\\"-b\\\" (path->string jar) \\\"-c\\\" (path->string jar)\\n                  u)])))\\n      (define next (and (< hop 6) (redirect-location raw)))\\n      (if next\\n          (loop (add1 hop) next)\\n          raw)))\\n\\n  (define (body-of raw)\\n    (match (regexp-match-positions #rx\\\"\\\\r?\\\\n\\\\r?\\\\n\\\" raw)\\n      [(cons _ end) (substring raw end)]\\n      [#f raw]))\\n\\n  ;; ------------------------------------------------------------ the flow\\n\\n  (printf \\\"Congame: ~a  instance: ~a~n~n\\\" base slug)\\n\\n  ;; Step 1: participant login lands on the introduction page.\\n  (define intro-res (request! \\\"GET\\\" (format \\\"~a/_anon-login/~a\\\" base slug) #f))\\n  (define intro (body-of intro-res))\\n  (check! (string-contains? intro \\\"Benchmark Study\\\")\\n          \\\"introduction page shows study title\\\")\\n  (check! (string-contains? intro \\\"Continue\\\")\\n          \\\"introduction page has a Continue button\\\")\\n  (check! (non-empty-string?\\n           (car-or-empty\\n            (regexp-match* #px\\\"<a [^>]*class=\\\\\\\"[^\\\\\\\"]*next-button[^\\\\\\\"]*\\\\\\\"[^>]*href=\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\" intro)))\\n          \\\"Continue link carries a continuation href\\\")\\n\\n  (define continue-href\\n    (or (regexp-match #px\\\"<a [^>]*class=\\\\\\\"[^\\\\\\\"]*next-button[^\\\\\\\"]*\\\\\\\"[^>]*href=\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\" intro)\\n        '(\\\"unresolvable\\\")))\\n\\n  ;; Step 2: click Continue -> name entry form.\\n  (define form-page\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"GET\\\" (resolve-url (second continue-href)) #f)))\\n\\n  (define form-action\\n    (regexp-match #px\\\"action=\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\" form-page))\\n\\n  (check! (and form-page (string-contains? form-page \\\"<form\\\")\\n               (string-contains? form-page \\\"display-name\\\"))\\n          \\\"name entry form rendered\\\")\\n\\n  (check! (not (string-null? (or (second (append form-action '(\\\"\\\" \\\"\\\"))) \\\"\\\")))\\n          \\\"form action extracted\\\")\\n\\n  ;; Step 3: empty submission must be rejected.\\n  (define rejected\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"POST\\\" (resolve-url (second (append form-action '(\\\"\\\" \\\"\\\"))))\\n                    \\\"display-name=&__tt=0&__ft=0\\\")))\\n  (check! (string-contains? rejected \\\"display-name\\\")\\n          \\\"still on the name entry form after empty submit\\\")\\n  (check! (not (string-contains? rejected \\\"All done\\\"))\\n          \\\"empty submit does not advance to final page\\\")\\n\\n  ;; Step 4: valid submission reaches the final page showing the name.\\n  (define tester \\\"Bench Tester\\\")\\n  (define finished\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"POST\\\" (resolve-url (second (append form-action '(\\\"\\\" \\\"\\\"))))\\n                    (format \\\"display-name=~a&__tt=0&__ft=0\\\" tester))))\\n  (check! (string-contains? finished \\\"All done!\\\")\\n          \\\"final page reached after submitting a name\\\")\\n  (check! (string-contains? finished tester)\\n          \\\"final page echoes the submitted name\\\")\\n\\n  ;; ------------------------------------------------------------- summary\\n\\n  (printf \\\"~n~a failures~n\\\" failures)\\n  (exit (if (zero? failures) 0 1))\\n  )\\n\",\"path\":\"/workspace/exercise.rkt\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":2308,"output":2289,"cacheRead":69888,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":814,"totalTokens":74485,"cost":{"input":0.00017309999999999998,"output":0.00057225,"cacheRead":0.00104832,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0017936699999999998}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"I'm making sloppy half-starts again — the file structure is getting confused. Let me carefully compose the complete, correct file in one go this time.\n\nDesign recap for `request!`:\n- For a GET: curl args = `-b jar -c jar url`\n- For a POST with form data: curl args = `-b jar -c jar --data-urlencode field=value url` (curl infers POST; use `-X POST` explicitly too)\n\nResponse handling: follow 30x redirects manually (parse Location), max ~6 hops. Return final raw response text. Then helpers:\n\n- `(split-headers-body res)` → two values: headers string, body string.\n- `(location-of res)`: find header line starting with \"Location:\" (case-insensitive) in headers block, strip value.\n- `(get! url)`: loop redirect following.\n- `(post! url field value)`: same loop.\n- Body extraction uses first blank-line separation (`\\r\\n\\r\\n` or `\\n\\n`). Use regexp-split #rx\"\\r?\\n\\r?\\n\" and take second element onward joined? Actually the response may have exactly one split → headers + body. Curl -i on HTTP/1.x normally yields full headers then body. Some servers chunked etc., but body = everything after first blank line. `regexp-match-positions` to find `\\r?\\n\\r?\\n`, substring after it.\n\nAssertions:\n\n1. After anon-login GET: body contains \"Benchmark Study\" (intro heading) AND regex next-button anchor href exists AND contains \">Continue<\".\n2. GET continue href: body contains \"<form\" and input name=\"display-name\", action URL captured from regex `<form[^>]*action=\"...\"`. Note paragraphify might mangle the form? Our step content is @md*{ ... @form[...] } — hmm wait, inside md rendering, does @form get preserved as xexpr? In cookbook they did exactly `@md{# Survey @form[survey-form on-submit render]}` so yes fine.\n\nBut careful: my render function is called by cgs:form internally (`(render rw)` returns xexpr), and the whole thing is embedded in the step's haml/md. The @md* wrapper wraps with div/container etc. The <form> tag survives.\n\n3. POST empty display-name=: expect 200 page still containing \"What is your name?\" or input, plus error message \"Please enter your name.\". Assert both.\n4. POST display-name=Bench Tester & __tt=0 __ft=0: follow redirects → body contains \"All done!\" and \"Bench Tester\".\n\nThen print total failures, exit code: exit non-zero if failures > 0 using (exit 1).\n\nEdge: URL resolution — continuation paths start with \"/\". prefix base when needed.\n\nAlso entity escaping: title \"All done!\" — exclamation fine. Name check: server escapes HTML of variable interpolation? If escaped, \"Bench Tester\" stays literal (space, no special chars). Good.\n\nOne subtlety: after failed validation POST, koyo's response could be a re-render via up-* ajax style? No—plain form POST without JS headers renders full page 200.\n\nAnother subtlety: form+submit binder sets defvar on success only.\n\nRegexes:\n- continue button: #px\"<a [^>]*class=\\\"[^\\\"]*next-button[^\\\"]*\\\"[^>]*href=\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"\"  — attr order class before href (as constructed). Also capture more generically: find all anchors and pick one whose attrs contain next-button; simpler single regex works given deterministic haml output ordering. But paragraphify swallows 'a' tags wholesale (swallow? includes a), preserving attributes — yes.\n- form action: #px\"action=\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"\"\n- verify input present: substring \"display-name\"\n\nLet me now write the final file completely and correctly."}}
