{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":1,"delta":"{\"path\":\"/workspace/exercise.rkt\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\": \"  (define continue-target\\n    (for/first ([anchor (in-list (regexp-match* #px\\\"<a [^>]*>\\\" intro #:gap-order? #f))])\\n      #f))\\n  ;; Simpler direct extraction: next-button anchor with href after its class.\\n  (set! continue-target\\n        (regexp-match #px\\\"class=\\\\\\\"[^\\\\\\\"]*next-button[^\\\\\\\"]*\\\\\\\"[^>]*href=\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\" intro))\", \"newText\": \"  ;; The Continue button renders as <a class=\\\"button next-button\\\" ... href=\\\"...\\\">;\\n  ;; haml emits attributes in construction order, so href follows its class.\\n  (define continue-target\\n    (regexp-match #px\\\"class=\\\\\\\"[^\\\\\\\"]*next-button[^\\\\\\\"]*\\\\\\\"[^>]*href=\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\" intro))\"}, {\"oldText\": \"  (define form-page\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"GET\\\" (resolve-url (second continue-target)) #f)))\\n\\n  (define form-action-m\\n    (regexp-match #px\\\"<form[^>]*action=\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\" form-page))\\n\\n  (check! (and (string-contains? form-page \\\"<form\\\")\\n               (string-contains? form-page \\\"input\\\")\\n               (string-contains? form-page \\\"display-name\\\"))\\n          \\\"name entry form rendered\\\")\\n  (check! (and form-action-m (non-empty-string? (second form-action-m)))\\n          \\\"form action extracted\\\")\\n\\n  ;; Step 3: empty submission must be rejected.\\n  (define rejected\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"POST\\\"\\n                    (resolve-url (second form-action-m))\\n                    \\\"display-name=&__tt=0&__ft=0\\\")))\", \"newText\": \"  (check! (and continue-target (non-empty-string? (second continue-target)))\\n          \\\"Continue link carries a continuation href\\\")\\n\\n  (define form-page\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"GET\\\"\\n                    (resolve-url (if continue-target (second continue-target) base))\\n                    #f)))\\n\\n  (define form-action-m\\n    (regexp-match #px\\\"<form[^>]*action=\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\" form-page))\\n\\n  (check! (and (string-contains? form-page \\\"<form\\\")\\n               (string-contains? form-page \\\"display-name\\\"))\\n          \\\"name entry form rendered\\\")\\n  (check! (and form-action-m (non-empty-string? (second form-action-m)))\\n          \\\"form action extracted\\\")\\n\\n  (define action-url\\n    (resolve-url (if form-action-m (second form-action-m) base)))\\n\\n  ;; Step 3: empty submission must be rejected.\\n  (define rejected\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"POST\\\" action-url\\n                    \\\"display-name=&__tt=0&__ft=0\\\")))\"}, {\"oldText\": \"  (define tester \\\"Bench Tester\\\")\\n  (define finished\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"POST\\\"\\n                    (resolve-url (second form-action-m))\\n                    (format \\\"display-name=~a&__tt=0&__ft=0\\\" tester))))\", \"newText\": \"  (define tester \\\"Bench Tester\\\")\\n  (define finished\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"POST\\\" action-url\\n                    (format \\\"display-name=~a&__tt=0&__ft=0\\\" tester))))\"}]}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":2731,"output":1348,"cacheRead":75072,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":506,"totalTokens":79151,"cost":{"input":0.00020482499999999998,"output":0.000337,"cacheRead":0.00112608,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.001667905}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Remaining\n issues\n in\n this\n file\n:\n\n1\n.\n The\n\n \n\n`\ncontinue\n\n\n-target\n\n\n`\n\n mess\n:\n\n `\n\nfor\n\n\n/first\n\n\n\n \n\n\n[\nanchor\n\n\n ...\n\n]`)\n\n\n\nthat\n\n\n returns\n\n\n #\nf\n\n \n\nis\n\n\n dead\n-weight\n,\n and\n\n \n\n`\n#:\n\ngap\n-order\n?\n\n#\n\nf\n\n\n`\n\n isn't\n\n \n\na\n\n\n valid\n option\n for\n \nregexp\n-match\n*\n (\noptions\n are\n \n#:name-value-pairs?\n\n )\n—\nwill\n likely\n compile\n (keyword\n args\n \nmay\n error\n at\n expansion?\n regexp\n-match\n*\n has\n \nkey\nword\n \narg\n \n#:gap-order??\n Actually\n \nracket\n's\n regexp\n-match\n* \n \naccepts\n #:gap-select?/\n \n#:match-select?\n/#\n:name\n-value\n-pairs? —\n#:gap-order?\n isn't one;\n unknown keyword arg →\n \ncompile\n \nerror).\n\n Also\n \nthe \nfirst \n`\nset!\n continue-target\n \n`; second set! pattern \nis fine\n but ugly.\n \nFix\n:\n replace whole block with single\n `\n(define continue-target (regexp-match ...))`.\n\n2\n.\n\n `(second form-action-m)`\n used later — if match fails, crash. Acceptable for exercise script; but guard better: use \n`\n(or form-action-m '( \"\" \"NO-ACTION\"))`. Simplify:\n \n`(define action-url (if form-action-m (second form-action-m) #f))`\n then checks!s handle failures by aborting gracefully... Keep it simple but robust: define helper that safely pulls group.\n\n3\n.\n In step 3 & 4 requests I call resolve-url with the action string — should be absolute already (starts with /) so fine.\n\n4\n.\n `(exit ...)` inside module+ main works.\n\n5\n.\n status-code not present anymore ✓.\n\n6\n.\n `(string-foldcase line)` prefix check case-insensitive ✓.\n\n7\n.\n redirect-location when no blank line (bad response) uses fallback substring 0..len then string-split lines may yield weird results but harmless.\n\n8\n. In `request!`, cond on `[data-field ...]`: data-field is #f or string like \"display-name=...\" ✓. But GET after POST-redirect uses data-field #f ✓.\n\n9\n. Note: curl \"-X\" \"GET\" is fine.\n\nLet me clean up item 1 and 2 minimally with an edit."}}
