\n \nnew\n \none\n? Let me re-read current file state and clean up.\n\n\n2\n.\n After\n \nstep-1 GET:\n if body contains a meta-refresh / redirect page, follow the href\n \nto\n the study page. Detect via `href=\"...\"` of the :a#skip anchor or simply retry GET on `(/study ...)` URL\n from\n redirect-page target: `reverse-uri 'study-page slug` → path likely `/study/<slug>`.\n Sim\npler:\n after\n \nlogin,\n explicitly GET `{base}/study/{slug}` (that's what auth-manager lands on). The interstitial's anchor \"click here\" href points there anyway. To be robust, parse for meta content=\"N; url=...\" then follow; fallback direct fetch.\n\n\n3\n.\n Also handle possible 303/302 Location redirects generally (already done).\n\n\nLet me inspect actual bodies step by step manually with curl to confirm shapes before rewriting assertions."}}
