{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":2,"delta":"{\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env racket\\n#lang racket/base\\n\\n;; Exercises benchmark-study against the Congame server over HTTP.\\n;;\\n;; Flow checked:\\n;;   1. Anon login for the active instance -> introduction page w/ Continue.\\n;;   2. Continue -> name entry form.\\n;;   3. Empty name submission is rejected (validation error, stays on form).\\n;;   4. A real submission advances to a final page echoing the submitted name.\\n;;\\n;; Usage: racket exercise.rkt   (exits nonzero on any failure)\\n\\n(module+ main\\n  (require racket/match\\n           racket/system\\n           racket/port\\n           racket/list\\n           racket/file\\n           racket/string)\\n\\n  ;; --------------------------------------------------------------- config\\n\\n  (define base (or (getenv \\\"CONGAME_URL\\\")\\n                   \\\"http://host.docker.internal:45471\\\"))\\n  (define slug (or (getenv \\\"CONGAME_INSTANCE\\\")\\n                   \\\"bench-20260827t083933z-smoke--fdb568e7\\\"))\\n\\n  ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- utils\\n\\n  (define failures 0)\\n\\n  (define (check! ok? label)\\n    (printf \\\"~a ~a~n\\\" (if ok? \\\"PASS\\\" \\\"FAIL\\\") label)\\n    (unless ok?\\n      (set! failures (add1 failures))))\\n\\n  ;; Full HTTP response incl. headers due to -i.\\n  (define (curl . args)\\n    (with-output-to-bytes\\n      (lambda ()\\n        (apply system* \\\"/usr/bin/curl\\\" \\\"-sS\\\" \\\"--max-time\\\" \\\"30\\\" args))))\\n\\n  (define jar (make-temporary-file \\\"congame-bench-cookies~a\\\"))\\n  (file-or-directory-permissions jar 384) ; rw------- so the session stays private\\n\\n  ;; Make relative URLs absolute against the study base URL.\\n  (define (resolve-url url)\\n    (if (string-prefix? url \\\"http\\\")\\n        url\\n        (string-append base url)))\\n\\n  (define blank-line/c #rx\\\"\\\\r?\\\\n\\\\r?\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n  (define (headers-of raw)\\n    (match (regexp-match-positions blank-line/c raw)\\n      [(cons s _) (substring raw 0 s)]\\n      [#f raw]))\\n\\n  (define (body-of raw)\\n    (match (regexp-match-positions blank-line/c raw)\\n      [(cons _ e) (substring raw e)]\\n      [#f raw]))\\n\\n  ;; Next URL from a 30x Location header, if any.\\n  (define (location-of raw)\\n    (for*/first ([line (in-list (string-split (headers-of raw) \\\"\\\\r\\\\n\\\"))]\\n                 #:when (string-prefix? (string-foldcase line) \\\"location:\\\")\\n                 [value (in-value (resolve-url (string-trim (substring line 9))))]\\n                 #:when (non-empty-string? (substring line 9)))\\n      value))\\n\\n  ;; Target of a 200 HTML <meta http-equiv=\\\"refresh\\\" ...> interstitial, if any.\\n  (define (meta-refresh-of raw)\\n    (match (regexp-match\\n            #px\\\"<meta\\\\\\\\s+http-equiv=\\\\\\\"refresh\\\\\\\"[^>]*content=\\\\\\\"[^\\\\\\\"]*(?:url=)?([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\"\\n            raw)\\n      [(list _ target) (resolve-url target)]\\n      [_ #f]))\\n\\n  ;; One single HTTP round-trip.\\n  (define (roundtrip! method url data-field)\\n    (bytes->string/utf-8\\n     (cond\\n       [data-field\\n        (curl \\\"-X\\\" method \\\"--data-urlencode\\\" data-field\\n              \\\"-b\\\" (path->string jar) \\\"-c\\\" (path->string jar)\\n              url)]\\n       [else\\n        (curl \\\"-X\\\" method\\n              \\\"-b\\\" (path->string jar) \\\"-c\\\" (path->string jar)\\n              url)])))\\n\\n  ;; Request a URL as a browser would: send the original request (with form\\n  ;; body, if given), then keep GETting whatever the server points us at --\\n  ;; via Location headers or login interstitials -- but never re-submits the\\n  ;; form body on the way. Only the final response text is returned.\\n  (define (request! method url [data-field #f])\\n    (let go ([hops 10] [u url] [body data-field])\\n      (when (zero? hops)\\n        (error 'request! \\\"too many redirects for ~a\\\" url))\\n      (define raw (roundtrip! method u body))\\n      (define next (or (location-of raw) (meta-refresh-of raw)))\\n      (cond\\n        [next (go (sub1 hops) next #f)]\\n        [else raw])))\\n\\n  ;; ----------------------------------------------------------- the flow\\n\\n  (printf \\\"Congame: ~a  instance: ~a~n~n\\\" base slug)\\n\\n  ;; Step 1: participant login lands on the introduction page.\\n  (define intro (body-of (request! \\\"GET\\\" (format \\\"~a/_anon-login/~a\\\" base slug))))\\n  (check! (string-contains? intro \\\"Benchmark Study\\\")\\n          \\\"introduction page shows the study title\\\")\\n  (check! (string-contains? intro \\\"Continue\\\")\\n          \\\"introduction page has a Continue button\\\")\\n\\n  ;; The Continue button renders as <a class=\\\"button next-button\\\" ... href=\\\"...\\\">\\n  ;; with haml emitting attributes in construction order, so href follows class.\\n  (define continue-target\\n    (regexp-match\\n     #px\\\"class=\\\\\\\"[^\\\\\\\"]*next-button[^\\\\\\\"]*\\\\\\\"[^>]*href=\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\"\\n     intro))\\n\\n  (check! (and continue-target (non-empty-string? (second continue-target)))\\n          \\\"Continue link carries a continuation href\\\")\\n\\n  ;; Step 2: click Continue -> name entry form.\\n  (define form-page\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"GET\\\"\\n               (resolve-url (if continue-target (second continue-target) base)))))\\n  (check! (and (string-contains? form-page \\\"<form\\\")\\n               (string-contains? form-page \\\"display-name\\\"))\\n          \\\"name entry form rendered\\\")\\n\\n  (define form-action-m\\n    (regexp-match #px\\\"<form[^>]*action=\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\" form-page))\\n  (check! (and form-action-m (non-empty-string? (second form-action-m)))\\n          \\\"form action extracted\\\")\\n\\n  (define action-url\\n    (resolve-url (if form-action-m (second form-action-m) base)))\\n\\n  ;; Step 3: empty submission must be rejected.\\n  (define rejected\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"POST\\\" action-url \\\"display-name=&__tt=0&__ft=0\\\")))\\n  (check! (string-contains? rejected \\\"What is your name?\\\")\\n          \\\"empty submit stays on the name entry form\\\")\\n  (check! (string-contains? rejected \\\"<ul class=\\\\\\\"errors\\\\\\\">\\\")\\n          \\\"empty submit rejected with a validation error\\\")\\n  (check! (not (string-contains? rejected \\\"All done\\\"))\\n          \\\"empty submit does not reach the final page\\\")\\n\\n  ;; Step 4: whitespace-only submission must be rejected too.\\n  (define rejected-blank\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"POST\\\" action-url \\\"display-name=%20%20%20&__tt=0&__ft=0\\\")))\\n  (check! (not (string-contains? rejected-blank \\\"All done\\\"))\\n          \\\"whitespace-only name does not reach the final page\\\")\\n\\n  ;; Step 5: valid submission reaches the final page showing the name.\\n  (define tester \\\"Bench Tester\\\")\\n  (define finished\\n    (body-of\\n     (request! \\\"POST\\\" action-url\\n               (format \\\"display-name=~a&__tt=0&__ft=0\\\" tester))))\\n  (check! (string-contains? finished \\\"All done!\\\")\\n          \\\"final page reached after submitting a name\\\")\\n  (check! (string-contains? finished tester)\\n          \\\"final page echoes the submitted name\\\")\\n\\n  ;; ------------------------------------------------------------- summary\\n\\n  (printf \\\"~n~a failures~n\\\" failures)\\n  (exit (if (zero? failures) 0 1))\\n  )\\n\",\"path\":\"/workspace/exercise.rkt\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":126,"output":3145,"cacheRead":90944,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1351,"totalTokens":94215,"cost":{"input":0.00000945,"output":0.00078625,"cacheRead":0.00136416,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00215986}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Also\n the\n exercise\n\n's\n\n step\n-1\n check\n must\n\nhandle\n\n \n\nthe\n inter\nstitial\n page\n\n \n\n(m\neta\n-refresh\n \n200\n response\n followed\n by\n\n manual\n\n \n\nGET\n\n\n of\n \n/\nstudy\n\n/s\nlug\n).\n Currently\n\n `\n\nrequest\n!\n\n`\n\n only\n follows\n\n\n\n \n \nHTTP\n Location\n \nredirect\ns\n,\n which\n\n \nthe\n \n\ninter\nstitial\n lacks\n.\n\n Fix\n:\n\n in\n\n `request\n!\n`,\n after\n\n redirect\ns\n end\n,\n\n if\n\n body\n contains\n\n\n meta\n http-equiv\n=\"\nrefresh\n \n...\"\n\n with\n \nurl\n=\n.../t\narget\n\n or\n a\n follow\n-on\n \nhref\n\n from\n \n#skip\n anchor\n,\n \nfollow\n\n \n\nonce\n.\n\n\n Simplest\n robust\n approach\n:\n give\n \nrequest\n!\n\n an\n extra\n \n\"soft\n-redirect\"\n phase\n:\n\n parse\n both\n patterns\n:\n\n\n-\n meta\n refresh\n: `\n#\n\npx\n\"http\n-equiv\n=\\\"refresh\n\\\"[^\n>]\n*content\n=\\\"[0\n-\n9]+\n;\n ([\n^\\\n\"]+)\n\\\"\" \n\n\n—\n\n \nin\n our\n server\n\n output\n\n it\n\n was\n\n\n content\n=\"\n3;\n /\nstudy\n/\n...\n\"\n\n\n(\nspace\n-sep\narated\n,\n no\n \nurl\n= prefix\n).\n\n Cover\n variants\n: regex\n `` + #px\"content=\\\"[^\\\"]*(?:url=)?([^\\\"]+)\\\"\" ```\n restricted\n to\n meta\n-refresh\n tags\n.\n\n\n\n-\n skip\n anchor\n fallback\n not\n needed\n if\n meta\n works\n.\n\n\nBut\n \nonly\n \nfollow\n \none\n \nsoft\n redirect\n \nafter\n \nthe\n Location\n chain\n\n settles\n\n (\n\nto\n avoid\n loops\n on\n \na\n\n page\n \nthat\n \nself\n-refresh\nes\n).\n\n Also\n\n ensure\n\n we\n\n don't\n soft-follow\n\n when\n\n body\n already\n\n contains\n \ndesired\n \ncontent\n —\n harmless\n \nsince\n\n following\n again\n\n just\n\n re-fetches\n the\n \nstudy\n\n page\n\n which\n\n idemp\notently\n \nshows\n \ncurrent\n \nstep\n.\n\n\nHmm\n\n\n,\n\n careful\n:\n\n if\n \nfinal\n \nresponse\n \ncontains\n \nmeta-refresh\n \n(they\n don't\n elsewhere)\n fine.\n\n\nLet\n \nme\n \nrewrite\n \n`request\n!`\n:\n\n```\nr\nacket\n\n\n(define\n (soft\n-target\n raw)\n\n \n (\nmatch\n (\nregexp\n-match\n #\npx\n\"http\n-equiv\n=\\\"\nrefresh\n\\\"\n[^\n>]\n*\ncontent\n=\\\"\n[0\n-\n9]+\n\\\\s\n*;\n\\\\s\n*(?:url\n=\n)?([\n^\\\n\"]\n+)\n\\\"\n\"\n raw\n))\n\n   \n [(\nlist\n _\n t\n)\n (\nresolve\n-url\n t\n)]\n\n   \n [\n_\n #\nf\n]))\n\n\n(define\n (request\n!\n method\n url\n data\n-field\n)\n\n\n \n\n (\nlet\n next\n ([hop\n \n0]\n [u\n url])\n)\n\n\n     \n ...\n existing\n loop\n →\n rename\n inner\n let\n loop\n\n )\n\n\n then\n\n\n \n outer\n\n:\n\n (\ndefine\n final\n-res\n ...\n)\n\n\n```\n\n\nClean\ner\n structure\n:\n\n```\nr\nacket\n\n\n(define\n (raw-request!\n method\n url\n data\n-field\n raw)\n ...)\n ;\n single\n HTTP\n round-trip\n\n(define\n (request\n!\n method\n url\n data\n-field\n)\n\n\n \n\n ;;\n hard\n redirects\n via\n Location\n\n \n (let\n go1\n ([hop\n \n0]\n [u\n url])\n)\n\n\n  \n\n (\ndefine\n raw\n (single\n-request\n method\n u\n data\n-field\n))\n\n\n   ...\n\n    \n (\ncond\n [(\nand\n (<\n hop\n \n6)\n (\nredirect\n-location\n raw))\n =>\n (\nλ\n (next)\n (\ngo1\n (\nadd1\n hop)\n next))]\n\n\n          [\nelse\n (\nlet\n go2\n ([n\n \n2]\n [u2\n u])\n ;\n\n\n soft\n meta\n-refresh\n following\n\n\n            \n (\ndefine\n m-target\n (soft\n-target\n raw))\n ]\n\n\n hmm getting convoluted\n with define-in-cond\n```\n\n\nLet me just write it plainly with an outer let and tail recursion over a combined \"how to continue\" resolver function, keeping runtime simple. Structure:\n\n```\nr\nacket\n\n(define (request! method url data-field)\n  (let go ([hops 10] [u url])\n    (unless (> hops 0) (error \"too many redirects\"))\n    (define raw (single-request method u data-field))\n    (cond\n      [(redirect-location raw)\n       => (λ (loc) (go (sub1 hops) loc))]\n      [(and (not (equal? u base)) (string-foldcase-in? ... )) ...) ; unnecessary\n      ;; soft redirect?\n      [(soft-refresh-target raw)\n       => (λ (tgt) (if (= hops 1) raw (go (sub1 hops) tgt)))]  \n        \n        ; guard against infinite soft-refresh loops:\n        only follow once per go level; since each following reduces hops to min 1, loop risk = 9 refreshes. A static page wouldn't reference itself.\n      [else raw])))\n```\n\nHmm—but there's subtlety: soft-refresh followed twice would repeat at levels where refresh appears. Since target pages won't have meta-refresh, a couple iterations terminate quickly.\n\nEdge concern: `data-field` should be dropped after first hop? On a 302 redirect curl clients typically convert POST→GET; my manual follower keeps calling single-request with data-field non-empty for subsequent GET hops, causing weird double submits. Location targets are plain study URLs; re-POSTing them is a real hazard (double submission of form action continuations!).\n\nSo: after the FIRST request, drop data-field regardless (standard browser semantics: redirects become GET). Implement: `(let go ([hops N] [u url] [field data-field]) ... (go (- hops 1) loc #f))`. First hop uses field; later hops none. That matches browsers (303 See Other → GET).\n\nThen empty-submit test will work as before because its direct 200 response has no redirect.\n\nOne more check: valid submit responds 302 → GET /study/slug renders final page ✓.\n\nNow also update the rejected-message assertion? It already checks \"Please enter your name.\" which now holds for BOTH empty (required message) and whitespace-only (my validator) paths.\n\nRewrite exercise.rkt fully one more time with these fixes, carefully."}}
