tch\n-positions\n; fine\n.\n\n4\n.\n\n meta-refresh regex:\n our interstitial markup:\n `<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"3; /study/bench...\" />`.\n My regex: `<meta\\s+http-equiv=\"refresh\"[^>]*content=\"[^\"]*(?:url=)?([^\"]+)\"`.\n For content\n=\"3;\n\n /study/\n...\"\n: `[^\"]*` would greedily consume everything including target INSIDE before group? Let's trace: pattern requires after opening quote: `[^\"]*(?:url=)?([^\"]+)` — first `[^\"]*` is greedy\n, backtracks so capture holds nonempty suffix. With input `3; /study/x`: greedy[^\"]* would take all\n, then require optional url=\n + capture [^\"]+: backtrack until capture succeeds with at least one char; no requirement of url=\n, so capture ends up being last char `/x`?? Actually entire `content\n=\"...\n\"`\n value chars are consumed by either lazy/greedy split: greedy consumes as much while leaving ≥1 char for capture → capture \n=\n final character \"x\". BAD.\n\n\nFix regex precisely:\n support forms:\n   - `3; /path`\n   - `3; url=/path`\nPattern within content value: `\\d+\\s*;\\s*(?:url\\s*=\\s*)?(.*)\"` with capture group continuing to closing quote:\n#px\"<meta\\\\s+http-equiv=\\\"refresh\\\"[^>]*content=\\\"[^\\\"]*?\\\\d+\\\\s*;\\\\s*(?:url\\\\s*=\\\\s*)?([^\\\"]+)\\\"\"\nThis makes prefix lazy `[^\\\"]*?\\d+\\s*;\\s*` hmm prefix must contain the digit... Let's simply match: content=\"\\s*[0-9]+\\s*;\\s*(?:url=)?([^\"]+)\":\n \nnum part directly after quote. Our server emits exactly `3; /study/...`. Simplify:\n#px\"<meta\\\\s+http-equiv=\\\"refresh\\\"[^>]*content=\\\"\\\\s*[0-9]+\\\\s*;\\\\s*(?:url=)?([^\\\"]+)\\\"\"\n✓ matches standard.\n\n\n5\n.\n\n The step-id continuation URLs contain `%22k%22` etc.; query junk fine.\n\n\n6\n.\n\n `blank-line/c #rx\"\\r?\\n\\r?\\n\"` — since response bodies are large HTML without \\r\\n header separators mostly (Server sends \\r\\n in headers per curl -i). Fine.\n\n\n7\n.\n\n In step\n3 rejected body assert \"<ul class=\\\"errors\\\">\":\n earlier obse