{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":635,"output":804,"cacheRead":120640,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":717,"totalTokens":122079,"cost":{"input":0.000047625,"output":0.00020099999999999998,"cacheRead":0.0018095999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.002058225}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Nearly green. One FAIL:\n\n\"empty submit rejected with a validation error\" — checks that the re-rendered form contains `\"Please enter your name.\"`.\n\nReason: The EMPTY value path goes through `binding/text` → `#f` → `(required #:message \"Please enter your name.\")`. Wait, I DID add `#:message \"Please enter your name.\"` to the study and... but did the SERVER get the updated study? I uploaded BEFORE making the `#:message` edit! The server is running the older build where `(required)` shows \"This field is required.\"\n\nBut wait — in my earlier manual curl session, empty submit showed `<ul class=\"errors\"><li>This field is required.</li></ul>`. Yes — old build.\n\nAlso, does forms-lib's `required` with `#:message` work as expected? Check signature: `(define ((required #:message [message #f]) v) ...)` — yes, and it uses `(or message (translate 'err-required))`. So new message will be \"Please enter your name.\"\n\nOptions:\na) Re-upload study (needed anyway for the `#:message` change) then re-run exercise.\nb) Relax assertion to accept either message.\n\nRe-upload is required regardless (study changed since upload). Let me re-upload now (with TMPDIR=/tmp), then re-run exercise without rebuilding? Exercise unchanged; just run it again against updated instance code.\n\nNote: uploading updates the SOURCE of the study on the server; the active instance may need... in congame, instances reference a study version; `raco congame upload` creates a new version, but EXISTING instances typically keep running the version they were created with! Hmm — that matters: the active instance slug may still serve the OLD compiled study.\n\nLet me check: congame-cli upload-study → POST /admin/studies/{id}/upload or similar updating source and maybe republishing. How do existing instances pick up new versions? In congame-web admin, when you update a study, you can \"deploy\"/publish a new version, and existing instances stay tied to versions unless upgraded. Hmm.\n\nFrom congame docs (introduction.scrbl / deployment): Uploaded studies create a new *version*; *instances* pin to a version; there might be an automatic behavior: if the instance was created before ANY version existed, maybe it uses latest? Unclear.\n\nEarlier, my exercise worked against the ORIGINAL placeholder?? Actually no—initial runs failed to find pages because... first real interactive-ish test showed MY study live (\"Benchmark Study\" intro). That upload happened after writing my full study.rkt v1. So instance picked up newly-uploaded version even though instance existed BEFORE upload (created by benchmark harness). So either the harness pre-created an instance with no version, or upload promotes/repoints instances.\n\nEither way: after re-upload with the message change, re-running will tell us. If the error message assertion still fails showing \"This field is required.\", then instance pinned and I should consider adapting: either relax assertion or ALSO make study robust... can't control instance pinning from study side.\n\nBetter: verify what the server serves post-upload; adjust exercise assertion to check presence of `<ul class=\"errors\">` AND/OR the specific message. The important spec requirement is non-empty enforcement — already covered by other assertions (empty/whitespace don't advance). The exact message text is cosmetic.\n\nBut I DO want the nicer unified message if the server supports it. Re-upload & see."}}
